    "description": "<div class=\"aakash-product-content\">\r\\n<h3>ZeroB AS1 - Water Softener-1000LPH</h3>\r\\nThe ZeroB AS1 conditions incoming hard water into a softer form at flow rates of 1000 LPH, improving the experience of bathing, washing and laundering while eliminating scum formation and scaling effects of hard water on appliances and bathroom accessories.\r\\n<h4>Key Features</h4>\r\\n<ul>\r\\n \t<li>Fully automatic programmable process valve with zero manual intervention</li>\r\\n \t<li>Softens water and prevents scale, scum and corrosion damage to bathroom fittings and appliances</li>\r\\n \t<li>Reduces detergent and soap consumption while protecting fabric colour and texture</li>\r\\n \t<li>Increases the lifespan of washing machines, water heaters and other appliances</li>\r\\n \t<li>Uses ZeroB's proprietary Purple Resin Media (RESIN Technology)</li>\r\\n</ul>\r\\n<h4>Technical Specifications</h4>\r\\n<table>\r\\n<tbody>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Water Flow</td>\r\\n<td>1000 LPH</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Dimensions (L*W*H)</td>\r\\n<td>330*470*660 mm</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Inlet Water Pressure (Min-Max)</td>\r\\n<td>1.5 to 3.5 kg/cm2</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Inlet Max Hardness (As CaCO3)</td>\r\\n<td>800 ppm</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Treated Hardness (As CaCO3)</td>\r\\n<td>&lt;50 ppm</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Inlet/Outlet Connection Size</td>\r\\n<td>1 inch</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Drain Line</td>\r\\n<td>0.5 inch</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Electric Supply</td>\r\\n<td>230 V AC/6 Amp, 1 point electric</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Treated Water Output at 500 ppm</td>\r\\n<td>800 liters</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Salt Tank Capacity</td>\r\\n<td>20 kg</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Purple Resin Quantity</td>\r\\n<td>12.5 liters</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Installation Footprint</td>\r\\n<td>Table top</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Process Valve</td>\r\\n<td>Fully Automatic Programmable</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n<tr>\r\\n<td>Salt per Recharge</td>\r\\n<td>2 kg</td>\r\\n</tr>\r\\n</tbody>\r\\n</table>\r\\n&nbsp;\r\\n\r\\n</div>",
